{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>These are the families of the Reubenite.</b> The insertion of the letters yod and heh of the Name does not occur here for any tribe except Reuben, Simeon, and Zebulun. For Reuben and Simeon — in order to appease their feelings and draw them near, after they had been reproved: Reuben for disturbing his father's bed, and Simeon for the deed of Zimri. And Zebulun — because he goes many times into a place of danger, as it is written: ״זבולון עם חרף נפשו למות״ (Zebulun, a people that exposes its soul to death)."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:46.292272722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}